# Per-MCP env for the crm drop-in. When this folder lands under
# ${MCP_DROPIN_DIR}/crm/ (typically via `cp -r examples/demos/crm
# customer-mcps/crm` in dev, or a Dockerfile COPY line in prod), the
# connector's drop-in scanner loads this file into the crm child's
# environment only. Never mutates process.env for other MCPs.
#
# The crm MCP is a thin client over the mock customer service at
# examples/mock-backend/. Override the URL if you run the mock on a
# different port / host / Fly private DNS name.
#
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored). In dev the mock listens on 7400 by default.

# Local dev:
# MOCK_CUSTOMERS_URL=http://localhost:7400

# Fly.io production (mock deployed as a private-only sibling app):
# MOCK_CUSTOMERS_URL=http://<mock-app>.internal:7400

# Controller-supplied creds win on conflict — this file is a dev escape
# hatch, not the production shape.
